From b25a804f506eb6be29caf67a2d20b671bb884521 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 11:52:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] desktop: pause window CSS animations while the
 system is idle

An unwatched Desktop window kept WindowServer, the GPU helper and the
renderer recompositing at the display refresh rate all night for one
spinner.

Measured on daveey-mini 2026-11-13 03:36-03:47 PST (card
t_01a1d4b6c5c7d552): HID idle ~5000 s, display set to never sleep,
Desktop window visible but unfocused. 60 s CPU-time deltas: WindowServer
44.7%, Desktop GPU helper 9.6%, renderer 12.9%, main 3.8% of a core. The
host's CPU governor was holding work for being >90% busy at the time.

Five whys:
1. Why is WindowServer at ~45% with nobody there? The Desktop window
   commits a new frame every refresh, and WindowServer recomposites it.
2. Why does the window commit frames? A 15 s V8 CPU profile of the
   renderer was 96.1% (idle): JS is not the source. document.getAnimations()
   listed one running animation: the 22 px `codicon-modifier-spin`
   spinner of the status-bar core-update chip ("Building update...").
3. Why is it running for so long? A core-update prebuild takes ~40 min
   (build_seconds 2316) and repeats after failures, and busy-session
   spinners do the same overnight; an infinite CSS animation asks for a
   frame every refresh regardless of whether anyone is looking.
4. Why does nothing stop it? Chromium only throttles hidden or occluded
   windows; a visible window on a display that never sleeps is neither.
5. Why no idle gate? Nothing in Desktop considered user presence for
   rendering.

Fix: electron/idle-motion-pause.ts polls powerMonitor.getSystemIdleTime()
(every 30 s while active, every 1 s while paused). After 300 s with no
keyboard/mouse input it insertCSS()es
`*, *::before, *::after { animation-play-state: paused !important; }` into
every window; any input removes it again within a second. Windows that load
or reload while paused get it re-applied (did-finish-load). Paused
animations need no frames, so the window stops repainting. Transitions and
JS-driven updates (streamed text) are untouched; an unreadable idle time
never pauses.

main.ts stays under its FILE_LINES cap: the wiring is one line, and its
private one-use `sleep()` helper is replaced by node:timers/promises'
setTimeout (same behaviour: resolve after ms).

Tests: electron/idle-motion-pause.test.ts (6 cases: active, pause/resume,
no stacking, reload/new window re-apply, destroyed/failed insertCSS,
unreadable idle time, timer cadence through attachIdleMotionPause).
RED: module missing; GREEN: 6/6. tsc -p tsconfig.electron.json clean.
